00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:02.200
Is it?

601
00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.160
I think so.

602
00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:03.440
In the credits?

603
00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:04.060
No.

604
00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:04.760
Oh my gosh.

605
00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.580
I'd have to look.

606
00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:06.040
I think so.

607
00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.020
Because in the script, your character's name is Steve.

608
00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:09.780
Yeah.

609
00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:10.320
In the script.

610
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.340
I feel like I need to check on IMDb.

611
00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:13.980
Yeah.

612
00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.400
You are credited as Asian Jim Halpert.

613
00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.000
Oh my gosh.

614
00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:19.120
Yes.

615
00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:20.680
Yes.

616
00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:22.080
That's, that is true.

617
00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.040
That's crazy.

618
00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:23.440
Yeah.

619
00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:23.860
Yeah.

620
00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:27.340
And I think, gosh, I should track down those scripts.

621
00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:28.900
I'm bringing up the script right now.

622
00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:29.040
Oh, you are.

623
00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.080
Wait for it.

624
00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:30.460
Okay.

625
00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.800
Cold open, Dwight is at his desk.

626
00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:36.880
A 30-something guy who looks sort of like an Asian version of Jim approaches.

627
00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.880
In the script, your name is Asian Guy.

628
00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.620
And then Pam in the script calls you Steve.

629
00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:45.980
Oh, okay, okay, okay.

630
00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:46.700
Yeah.

631
00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:49.300
But you have all that dialogue about that.

632
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.300
I'm hoping for a voicemail from Paul.

633
00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:52.020
Krieger Murphy.

634
00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:52.780
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

635
00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:53.280
Krieger, yeah.

636
00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.040
Yeah.

637
00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.200
Oh, yeah, yeah.

638
00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.980
They kiss, Pam walks off.

639
00:19:57.940 --> 00:19:58.420
Amazing.

640
00:19:59.140 --> 00:19:59.620
Amazing.

641
00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.160
Do you get recognized from being on The Office?

642
00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.380
How has that plagued you?

643
00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.380
I mean, because people shout random things at us.

644
00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.440
Someone has shouted to me, green is whore-ish.

645
00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.120
I had on a green, like, tank top.

646
00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:14.960
And I was like, what?

647
00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.180
And then I'm like, oh, right.

648
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:26.200
Yeah, well, you know, I mean, it was after I filmed it and even after it aired, I didn't get recognized too much from it.

649
00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:36.620
But eventually, I would say several years later is when it became like a meme and when it started really circulating online.

650
00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:44.760
And that's when, yeah, people would, I think I was talking about it on Conan once where, you know, I had kind of forgotten about it.

651
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.620
Not forgotten about it, but it just wasn't top of mind.

652
00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.200
Sure, it was a long time ago.

653
00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:52.060
And somebody screamed out, hey, Asian Jim!

654
00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:55.760
And I, like, turned around and I thought it was, like, some, like, racial thing.

655
00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.780
Or I didn't know, you know, because I just didn't put it together.

656
00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:06.240
And then soon enough, yeah, I'd hear more Asian Jims and I'd go, okay, okay, it's online.

657
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:06.760
Yeah.

658
00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:07.680
It's online.

659
00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:16.840
And now, also, in some small way, you guys brought it back because you did this thing with John Krasinski for the trailer for his movie, right?

660
00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:17.880
Yes, for If.

661
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.520
That was so funny.

662
00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.380
How did you even do it?

663
00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.500
You're, like, pranking Ryan Reynolds.

664
00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.860
Because you're saying you are John Krasinski.

665
00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.480
And it kind of broke the internet.

666
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.360
People, like, went berserk for it.

667
00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:33.660
I mean, I think it was such a big thing online for so many years.

668
00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:38.580
And John was, you know, directing that movie and I don't know if it was Ryan or John.

669
00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:44.140
I think it might have been Ryan who thought, who came up with it and asked if I'd be down to do it.

670
00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.080
I'm like, yeah, of course.

671
00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:45.800
Of course.

672
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:46.080
Yeah.

673
00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:53.360
But you had to change your clothes, like, multiple times to be inserted into, like, scenes of you directing the movie.

674
00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:54.220
Yes.

675
00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:55.320
Yeah, that's right.

676
00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:55.920
That's right.

677
00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:56.500
It's really impressive.

678
00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.120
I just shot on a green screen in different outfits.

679
00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:06.940
And then they just kind of somehow put me in there, in these shots, BTS shots that they had made for the movie.

680
00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:07.620
It was crazy.

681
00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:08.640
It was fun.

682
00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:09.540
It was very fun.

683
00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.080
But, yeah, I mean, it just speaks to the power of the internet.

684
00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.180
It was just such a big thing.

685
00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:14.760
Yeah.

686
00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:15.360
Yeah.

687
00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:15.980
Yeah.

688
00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:26.040
And to this day, people are like, it's funny because it was such a big thing online that some people come up to me thinking that I was a regular on the show, you know,

689
00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.040
even though I wasn't.

690
00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:28.580
You know, it was just one scene.

691
00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.180
But you stole the scene, you know?

692
00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:35.680
I mean, that's all you can ever hope for, no matter, like, how big or small your role.

693
00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:39.340
Like, if you get that moment where you're like, I just owned that.

694
00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:39.780
Yeah.

695
00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:44.140
I mean, for me, literally on the day, it was just like, I'm just so happy to be a part of this.

696
00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:47.640
I'm just so happy to be on set, on this set in particular.

697
00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.120
And it was one of those, like, okay, that was great.

698
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:51.300
That was great.

699
00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:53.180
What's the next thing, you know?

700
00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:58.500
Well, we reunited after the office on Fresh Off the Boat, which was a really great show.

701
00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.880
Yeah, you did several episodes, right?

702
00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:01.500
I did, I did.

703
00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:05.180
I played Jessica, who's played by Constance Wu, like her nemesis.

704
00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:05.800
Her nemesis, yeah.

705
00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:07.360
Which is such, again, a bitch.

706
00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.600
Might have been typecasting.

707
00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:11.680
But that was super fun.

708
00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:12.320
Yeah, it was.

709
00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.320
And everybody there was so nice.

710
00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:17.160
And that was on for like six years, right?

711
00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:18.120
Six seasons, yeah.

712
00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.700
Yeah, that was great on ABC.

713
00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:20.660
It was great.

714
00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:21.720
It was super fun.

715
00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:23.620
And yeah, it was so great having you on.

716
00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:26.680
Yeah, I was just tripping that you were on the show.

717
00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.760
Because again, I was such a huge fan of the office.

718
00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:31.140
And yeah, it was very cool.

719
00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:35.680
I was really hoping that our, so that our two couples, I was hoping we had some more

720
00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.160
like double dates because that was really, those like dinner scenes were fun.

721
00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:39.640
Yeah.

722
00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:44.760
But Jenna and I have both just sort of been going over your filmography and watching all

723
00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:45.360
kinds of stuff.

724
00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:46.680
And we're such fans of yours.

725
00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:49.880
And I have something I want to talk about and you have something you want to talk about,

726
00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:51.460
but I want to go firSt.

727
00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:52.540
You can go firSt.

728
00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:52.860
Okay.

729
00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:58.500
So last night with my teenagers, we watch, because our producer, Matt Beagle was like,

730
00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:03.500
if you guys love rom-coms, you have to see Always Be My Maybe that you did.

731
00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:04.980
He couldn't be here today.

732
00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:08.020
And he wanted us to tell you it's his favorite rom-com.

733
00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:08.880
Oh my God.

734
00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:11.280
So I was like, I love a rom-com.

735
00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:12.500
I don't know how I miss that one.

736
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:13.300
I want to watch it.

737
00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:14.780
It's so good.

738
00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:15.780
You're so funny in it.

739
00:24:15.860 --> 00:24:17.540
There's so many funny people in this.

740
00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:18.980
And you know, Ali Wong is great.

741
00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:22.800
But for those of you who have listened to Office Ladies for a long time, you know that

742
00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:25.720
Jenna and I are slightly obsessed with Keanu Reeves.

743
00:24:26.260 --> 00:24:32.120
And you have a hilarious scene with Keanu Reeves and you punch him in the face.

744
00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:33.200
I punch him in the face.

745
00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:33.680
I do.

746
00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:34.020
Yeah.

747
00:24:34.240 --> 00:24:37.600
I'm sure you've talked about this a lot, but please, can you tell us everything about

748
00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:39.060
being in scenes and what was that like?

749
00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:42.140
And you're so funny in it and you get so pissed off at him.

750
00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:45.440
That was another surreal.

751
00:24:45.680 --> 00:24:50.720
I mean, you know, this job is just filled with surreal experiences, you know, as you guys

752
00:24:50.720 --> 00:24:51.000
know.

753
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.580
I should say Keanu plays himself, right?

754
00:24:54.100 --> 00:24:54.360
Yes.

755
00:24:54.620 --> 00:24:58.440
And he goes out on a date with the person that you're in love with.

756
00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:03.160
And you have to like, watch the person you love be on a date with Keanu Reeves.

757
00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:04.420
Yeah, we're on a double date.

758
00:25:04.560 --> 00:25:05.700
Yeah, on a double date.

759
00:25:05.880 --> 00:25:09.420
And both of the women, though, are just in love with Keanu Reeves.

760
00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.620
It's pretty real in that way, right?

761
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:13.080
Yeah.

762
00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:16.820
That whole project was so fun because I got to work with Ali, who's an old friend.

763
00:25:16.820 --> 00:25:21.640
And we wanted a celebrity cameo, you know, celebrity to play himself.

764
00:25:21.860 --> 00:25:26.400
And I believe we had a list of just like people who we thought we could get, you know, and they

765
00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:31.780
were all like people we loved, not nearly as famous as Keanu Reeves.

766
00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:38.420
And we presented that list to Netflix and Netflix was like, why don't you like dream bigger?

767
00:25:38.680 --> 00:25:40.380
You know, like who's the ideal?

768
00:25:40.600 --> 00:25:40.780
Yeah.

769
00:25:40.900 --> 00:25:42.860
And we were like, Keanu Reeves is the ideal.

770
00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:44.640
They're like, let's try for that.

771
00:25:45.480 --> 00:25:47.320
And we somehow got him.

772
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:52.980
He was like shooting John Wick at the time, but he had an opening and he loved the idea

773
00:25:52.980 --> 00:25:55.600
of playing himself in this, you know, rom-com.

774
00:25:55.800 --> 00:26:00.440
And he came out for a few days and in the Bay Area and he was just so incredibly nice.

775
00:26:00.620 --> 00:26:01.820
He's just like so kind.

776
00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:03.300
I mean, all the stories, you know.

777
00:26:03.300 --> 00:26:04.340
Isn't that everything you want to hear?

778
00:26:04.520 --> 00:26:04.800
Yes.

779
00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:06.620
Sam, are you so happy right now?

780
00:26:06.680 --> 00:26:07.400
I'm thrilled.

781
00:26:07.400 --> 00:26:14.440
Yeah, he was so kind, so open, just sharing so much of his life and his stories with us.

782
00:26:14.580 --> 00:26:17.940
And so game, you know, in the scenes, just coming up with pitches.

783
00:26:18.140 --> 00:26:22.320
There's a moment where he's wearing glasses and he takes them off and I put my fingers

784
00:26:22.320 --> 00:26:22.780
through the glass.

785
00:26:22.880 --> 00:26:24.600
I'm like, there's no lenses in these glasses.

786
00:26:24.620 --> 00:26:25.660
And he's like, I know.

787
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:27.720
And that was like his pitch, you know.

788
00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:29.620
He had a bunch of pitches like that.

789
00:26:29.740 --> 00:26:32.420
And yeah, it was just so fun and surreal.

790
00:26:32.420 --> 00:26:33.620
And we were doing overnights.

791
00:26:33.620 --> 00:26:38.040
So it was kind of like, you know, it's stressful to do overnights.

792
00:26:38.260 --> 00:26:40.280
But he was just so professional, you know.

793
00:26:40.480 --> 00:26:43.240
So like just down to play.

794
00:26:43.700 --> 00:26:44.080
Down to play.

795
00:26:44.400 --> 00:26:46.440
I do have to read one more thing.

796
00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:49.980
There is a song that you rap called I Punched Keanu Reeves.

797
00:26:50.480 --> 00:26:52.720
And this is like one of the best lyrics.

798
00:26:53.140 --> 00:26:56.300
You say, best believe I punched Keanu Reeves.

799
00:26:56.420 --> 00:26:59.200
And it was better than any scene you could see in Speed.

800
00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:02.220
I hit John Wick and now I'm feeling so appealing.

