I love you.

1317
00:46:32.590 --> 00:46:34.790
You two are sunshine to the world.

1318
00:46:35.110 --> 00:46:37.010
Aw, thanks so much.

1319
00:46:37.010 --> 00:46:37.970
That's so nice.

1320
00:46:38.410 --> 00:46:40.810
Gosh, a lot goes into all of that.

1321
00:46:41.010 --> 00:46:46.370
It is a little bit like a part-time job that gets attached to your full-time job.

1322
00:46:46.510 --> 00:46:48.510
The full-time job being making the show.

1323
00:46:48.670 --> 00:46:48.850
Right.

1324
00:46:48.930 --> 00:46:50.950
Or making a movie, whatever you made.

1325
00:46:51.130 --> 00:46:51.410
Mm-hmm.

1326
00:46:51.570 --> 00:46:55.310
There becomes this whole other job, which is promoting it,

1327
00:46:55.470 --> 00:46:58.790
getting the word out about it, creating promotional materials.

1328
00:46:58.790 --> 00:47:03.630
And you know, Kaden, depending on what project you're working on, there can be a whole team

1329
00:47:03.630 --> 00:47:06.590
of people assigned to the marketing.

1330
00:47:06.910 --> 00:47:12.670
So you might have a day where you go and you do a photo shoot, right?

1331
00:47:12.870 --> 00:47:14.330
With different people in the caSt.

1332
00:47:14.510 --> 00:47:19.670
And then also they might say, hey, could you guys take these phones and capture behind-the-scene

1333
00:47:19.670 --> 00:47:20.170
content?

1334
00:47:20.470 --> 00:47:23.630
Or they'll send someone to capture behind-the-scene content.

1335
00:47:23.630 --> 00:47:26.770
And then they use that and make it into little clips.

1336
00:47:26.990 --> 00:47:30.890
And then you have a day where you talk to people who write on magazines.

1337
00:47:30.890 --> 00:47:33.630
And then sometimes you go on TV shows, talk shows.

1338
00:47:34.070 --> 00:47:35.510
It's a whole machine.

1339
00:47:36.030 --> 00:47:36.570
Yeah.

1340
00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:43.830
Before every new season, they would arrange some sort of full-cast photo shoot on our set.

1341
00:47:44.010 --> 00:47:44.390
Mm-hmm.

1342
00:47:44.790 --> 00:47:49.790
And one year, they set up a bunch of paper boxes in the break room.

1343
00:47:49.790 --> 00:47:50.450
Yes.

1344
00:47:50.670 --> 00:47:52.310
And a lot of you have seen that picture.

1345
00:47:52.510 --> 00:47:52.810
Sure.

1346
00:47:53.010 --> 00:47:54.650
Trying to fit us all in that break room.

1347
00:47:54.750 --> 00:47:55.970
I don't think they thought that through.

1348
00:47:56.230 --> 00:48:01.650
Well, I think that's why maybe the following year, they put us all in the warehouse.

1349
00:48:01.790 --> 00:48:02.190
Warehouse.

1350
00:48:02.510 --> 00:48:02.690
Yes.

1351
00:48:02.890 --> 00:48:04.370
In front of a bunch of paper boxes.

1352
00:48:04.810 --> 00:48:06.910
But they would have us do a group photo.

1353
00:48:06.910 --> 00:48:08.670
They would put us in different pairings.

1354
00:48:08.850 --> 00:48:09.910
They would have single photos.

1355
00:48:10.110 --> 00:48:11.630
And that would be our morning.

1356
00:48:11.830 --> 00:48:17.630
We would spend four or five hours just cycling through doing promotional photos.

1357
00:48:17.630 --> 00:48:20.370
But we also had to be doing the show.

1358
00:48:21.130 --> 00:48:25.690
So if you weren't getting your picture taken, then you were shooting a scene.

1359
00:48:25.910 --> 00:48:31.350
And my goodness, if that wasn't a crazy scheduling job for Kelly Cantley and Rusty Mahmood, our

1360
00:48:31.350 --> 00:48:31.870
ADs.

1361
00:48:32.010 --> 00:48:35.830
And then also, you would have sort of like a full-on press junket day.

1362
00:48:35.990 --> 00:48:37.410
And you would get paired up with someone.

1363
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:39.330
Jenna, you and I would get paired up together.

1364
00:48:39.870 --> 00:48:42.610
And we would have to be on set super early.

1365
00:48:42.990 --> 00:48:45.010
You know, we would arrive at 3 a.m.

1366
00:48:45.810 --> 00:48:48.250
To be camera ready by 4 a.m.

1367
00:48:48.610 --> 00:48:48.910
Yeah.

1368
00:48:49.110 --> 00:48:50.650
And they'll sit you down in two chairs.

1369
00:48:50.650 --> 00:48:58.030
And then you are via satellite to all these different live morning news prograMs.

1370
00:48:58.410 --> 00:49:01.570
But those programs are starting on the East CoaSt.

1371
00:49:01.790 --> 00:49:02.030
Yeah.

1372
00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:03.270
As of 7 a.m.

1373
00:49:03.270 --> 00:49:05.230
And you have the little thing in your ear.

1374
00:49:05.490 --> 00:49:07.030
And you can hear the newscasters.

1375
00:49:07.110 --> 00:49:07.950
You can't see them.

1376
00:49:08.110 --> 00:49:09.310
You can hear them.

1377
00:49:09.790 --> 00:49:11.390
And they're asking you questions.

1378
00:49:11.390 --> 00:49:12.810
You do that for three minutes.

1379
00:49:12.810 --> 00:49:16.070
And they're like, okay, and now we're going to New Hampshire.

1380
00:49:16.250 --> 00:49:16.510
Yes.

1381
00:49:16.650 --> 00:49:18.710
There's someone standing on set with you.

1382
00:49:18.990 --> 00:49:22.570
And we often did these on the set of The Office as our backdrop.

1383
00:49:22.830 --> 00:49:27.430
But there was a person's role at NBC who would have a list of all the cities in the

1384
00:49:27.430 --> 00:49:30.350
United States that we'd be popping on to their morning show.

1385
00:49:30.770 --> 00:49:33.450
And they would say, all right, guys, up next, Toledo, Ohio.

1386
00:49:34.030 --> 00:49:37.210
In 3, 2, 1, you're live, right?

1387
00:49:37.390 --> 00:49:40.810
And then it would be like, up next, you're on with St. Louis, Missouri.

1388
00:49:41.130 --> 00:49:43.870
In 3, 2, 1, and on and on and on.

1389
00:49:43.990 --> 00:49:47.210
And by the end, you have no idea who you're talking to anymore.

1390
00:49:47.450 --> 00:49:51.250
And also, by the way, if you need to go to the bathroom, you got to hold it.

1391
00:49:51.670 --> 00:49:51.790
Yeah.

1392
00:49:51.970 --> 00:49:54.890
They would have little breaks that they would work in.

1393
00:49:54.990 --> 00:49:58.750
And there'd usually be a slightly larger break where you could get some breakfast while

1394
00:50:00.350 --> 00:50:04.030
West Coast news programs to start at actual 7 a.m.

1395
00:50:04.290 --> 00:50:08.230
And then after you did that, you started your regular workday.

1396
00:50:08.890 --> 00:50:09.110
Yeah.

1397
00:50:09.310 --> 00:50:13.730
So we would be there for three hours and then go into our regular workday.

1398
00:50:14.010 --> 00:50:16.130
And, you know, everyone was always so gracious.

1399
00:50:16.130 --> 00:50:24.970
But I do have a new appreciation for everyone that ever has to call in or pop in via satellite

1400
00:50:24.970 --> 00:50:28.230
to a talk show because there is that delay.

1401
00:50:28.490 --> 00:50:31.410
And I'm sure all of y'all listening have seen this before.

1402
00:50:31.710 --> 00:50:36.910
Someone's on your news program and they pop in and the person asks the question like,

1403
00:50:37.270 --> 00:50:40.830
all right, can you tell us about this new season of your TV show?

1404
00:50:40.830 --> 00:50:46.250
And then they're like, yes, I can't.

1405
00:50:46.370 --> 00:50:46.730
I'm sorry.

1406
00:50:46.970 --> 00:50:47.450
Yeah.

1407
00:50:47.730 --> 00:50:50.170
It's like so clunky sometimes.

1408
00:50:50.410 --> 00:50:51.610
And they haven't fixed that.

1409
00:50:51.910 --> 00:50:54.370
There's a delay and it's always a little tricky.

1410
00:50:54.630 --> 00:51:02.170
But anyway, it is a lot of moving parts the way shows and movies come together and the promotion.

1411
00:51:02.190 --> 00:51:04.830
I have a lot of respect for all the different departments.

1412
00:51:05.390 --> 00:51:05.570
Yeah.

1413
00:51:05.570 --> 00:51:10.510
But it has to get folded into your already very busy work week.

1414
00:51:10.570 --> 00:51:13.950
And all of that scheduling would have to go through the producers.

1415
00:51:14.770 --> 00:51:18.770
If someone needed to go do a taping of The Tonight Show,

1416
00:51:18.770 --> 00:51:23.250
we would have to move the whole schedule around because the rest of us would still be filming.

1417
00:51:23.550 --> 00:51:27.250
And none of those late night talk shows are filmed late at night.

1418
00:51:27.530 --> 00:51:28.250
That's correct.

1419
00:51:28.510 --> 00:51:30.190
They're filmed at like 5 p.m.

1420
00:51:30.310 --> 00:51:31.110
or 4 p.m.

1421
00:51:31.170 --> 00:51:32.630
You know, it's like late afternoon.

1422
00:51:33.430 --> 00:51:36.210
So a workday is still happening half the time.

1423
00:51:36.610 --> 00:51:39.130
Well, and one of the things that would be tricky for me,

1424
00:51:39.590 --> 00:51:43.530
and Angela, I'm sure this was true for you as well, not so much for the gentlemen,

1425
00:51:44.310 --> 00:51:45.630
but our hair.

1426
00:51:45.810 --> 00:51:46.490
Oh, gosh.

1427
00:51:46.590 --> 00:51:49.690
As our characters of Angela and Pam was very specific.

1428
00:51:49.990 --> 00:51:55.030
But if I was going to go be a guest on a late night talk show and wear like a cute little dress or

1429
00:51:55.030 --> 00:51:57.430
whatever, and, you know, it didn't work.

1430
00:51:57.950 --> 00:51:59.410
I would have to be de-Pam.

1431
00:51:59.410 --> 00:51:59.950
I know.

1432
00:52:00.130 --> 00:52:01.910
And you would have to be de-Angela Martin.

1433
00:52:01.910 --> 00:52:02.390
I know.

1434
00:52:02.570 --> 00:52:05.030
I didn't want to go on a late night talk show with a bun.

1435
00:52:05.230 --> 00:52:06.610
With a severe bun.

1436
00:52:07.290 --> 00:52:08.930
Maybe I should have one time.

1437
00:52:10.830 --> 00:52:14.750
Well, there was one thing, and I can't remember what it is now off the top of my head,

1438
00:52:15.250 --> 00:52:18.210
where we had something we had to go to, Angela.

1439
00:52:18.530 --> 00:52:23.850
I feel like it was a panel that we all had to talk on after work, but we went late.

1440
00:52:23.850 --> 00:52:31.230
And Kim Ferry was just like, Jenna, the best I can do is throw that hair up into like a crazy

1441
00:52:31.230 --> 00:52:32.330
ponytail for you.

1442
00:52:32.790 --> 00:52:34.610
Otherwise, you're going to have Pam hair.

1443
00:52:34.970 --> 00:52:36.190
I was like, do the ponytail.

1444
00:52:36.350 --> 00:52:37.030
Do the ponytail.

1445
00:52:37.030 --> 00:52:43.030
I went to an award show in my Angela Martin ponytail because we filmed so late.

1446
00:52:43.450 --> 00:52:43.790
Yes.

1447
00:52:43.970 --> 00:52:45.130
I can't remember which one it was.

1448
00:52:45.550 --> 00:52:45.930
I think it was the Golden Globes almoSt.

1449
00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:46.830
Was it the Golden Globes?

1450
00:52:46.850 --> 00:52:51.490
I was in a red dress, and I'm in my Angela Martin ponytail because I didn't have time.

1451
00:52:51.650 --> 00:52:52.850
With the swoop bang.

1452
00:52:53.110 --> 00:52:53.350
Yes.

1453
00:52:54.710 --> 00:52:55.970
Well, there you go.

1454
00:52:56.250 --> 00:52:57.850
Thanks for asking that question.

1455
00:52:57.850 --> 00:52:59.530
That's a little bit behind the scenes.

1456
00:53:00.130 --> 00:53:01.850
We love hearing from you guys.

1457
00:53:02.050 --> 00:53:04.950
I'll put a swipe up in our stories where you can write us.

1458
00:53:05.090 --> 00:53:09.790
And a huge thank you to Randall Park for coming into the studio with us today.

1459
00:53:10.070 --> 00:53:13.930
Yes, it was so generous of him to come in the studio and speak with us today.

1460
00:53:14.230 --> 00:53:15.030
Thank you, Randall.

1461
00:53:15.370 --> 00:53:17.110
Everyone, be sure to check him out.

1462
00:53:17.230 --> 00:53:18.290
He's everywhere, okay?

1463
00:53:18.530 --> 00:53:18.710
He is.

1464
00:53:18.870 --> 00:53:21.010
Look for him in AMC's The Audacity.

1465
00:53:21.010 --> 00:53:24.630
Look for him in these two indie films, Brian and Wishful Thinking.

1466
00:53:24.910 --> 00:53:27.590
And then, of course, there's the show that I am obsessed with.

1467
00:53:27.730 --> 00:53:31.570
I'm late to the party, but I'm obsessed, which is The Residence on Netflix.

1468
00:53:32.430 --> 00:53:36.690
And for you folks out there that love a rom-com as much as me and Matt Beagle, too,

1469
00:53:37.350 --> 00:53:41.010
check out his 2019 movie, Always Be My Maybe.

1470
00:53:41.310 --> 00:53:42.250
It's so fun.

1471
00:53:42.610 --> 00:53:44.770
And you get a little Keanu Reeves.

1472
00:53:44.970 --> 00:53:45.790
All right, everyone.

1473
00:53:45.990 --> 00:53:46.610
Thank you so much.

1474
00:53:46.690 --> 00:53:47.490
We'll see you next week.

1475
00:53:47.670 --> 00:53:48.230
See you then.

1476
00:53:48.650 --> 00:53:53.320
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

